1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Floating over the Nakagawa,
aiming for the setting sun,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes go flying too.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
Strutting along, I wonder,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,120
they laugh, saying I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I leave my energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
pachinko, a yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,160
The streets feel strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:07,440
From the pointed hat's water spout,
the sunset falls into the vast sky.

9
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:19,720
Tomorrow will end just like this, won't it?
In Katsushika Shibamata, happiness again.

10
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,440
After running around everywhere,
I finally realized.

11
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:24,680
Because I'm such a fool.

12
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:31,740
I'll stake my life! All-you-can-eat!

13
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:47,420
Well, I could go for something
sweet to go with my tea.

14
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,260
What do you think this is?

15
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:00,880
Alright, let's dig in.

16
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:02,820
Ryo-san!

17
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:04,340
I found an amazing bargain...

18
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:04,900
Later.

19
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:07,800
Daifuku, daifuku...

20
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:12,280
That was delicious.

21
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:23,060
What a restless fellow.

22
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:29,260
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

23
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:32,120
Who ate my daifuku?!

24
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:35,680
The daifuku's gone bad!

25
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,400
Chief

26
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:43,400
What are you doing?

27
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:45,360
It's nothing.

28
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:46,360
Chief.

29
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:50,660
Do you know where the daifuku
that was in the kitchen went?

30
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:53,700
I don't know anything about any daifuku.

31
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:54,540
Really?

32
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,240
I really don't know, so I don't know.

33
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:59,160
What on earth happened?

34
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:02,660
The daifuku I saved in
the kitchen has disappeared!

35
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:04,920
No way, I didn't eat it!

36
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,960
I don't know anything about that either.

37
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,120
So that means...

38
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:16,740
Go on, Chief, try making an excuse.

39
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:18,980
Come on now!

40
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:21,100
We'll just decide it's fine like this.

41
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,860
Why would you do something like that?

42
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:24,960
Is there some reason you can't?

43
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,500
No, there's no such reason.

44
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,260
Look!

45
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:32,920
Got you! Crumbs of smashed bean paste!

46
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:35,540
The culprit is the Chief!

47
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:39,740
What a shameless glutton.

48
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:44,160
Secretly eating all the daifuku your subordinates were looking forward to,
all by yourself!

49
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:46,180
Is that how a superior
is supposed to behave?

50
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:51,040
So the Chief is hogging
all the food in the box?

51
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:54,020
Well, if he'd at least left one behind...

52
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:56,600
But eating every last bit like that?

53
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:59,680
This is when your true character shows,
isn't it.

54
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:02,880
As a human being, I can't believe it.

55
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:05,640
You don't have to go that far, though.

56
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:06,900
That's right!

57
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:08,540
Anyway, that daifuku...

58
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:10,640
Reiko is the one who bought it, isn't she?

59
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:11,720
That's right.

60
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,880
It's not like it belongs to Ryo-chan,
you know.

61
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:18,560
That's cold.

62
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:20,660
Getting worked up only makes it worse.

63
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:23,520
In the end, I went and blew all my money.

64
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:25,100
and now there's nothing at all to eat.

65
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:26,380
Same old pattern

66
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:28,620
You didn't get any either, did you, senpai?

67
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:30,920
If only that daifuku had been left,

68
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:33,480
we'd have been fine.

69
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:36,600
To me, that thing was
worth ten thousand yen.

70
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:38,760
And then the Chief went and...

71
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,740
The Chief...

72
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:43,520
I never thought the Chief
would actually eat it!

73
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:46,440
I thought, at least not the Chief!

74
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:47,400
Aaah!

75
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:51,400
Honestly, I don't know who to trust anymore.

76
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,740
Ugh, I hate this, I really hate this.

77
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:53,140
Fine.

78
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:55,240
You'll pay us back for the daifuku, right?

79
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,280
Daifuku?

80
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:58,060
You don't get it, do you?

81
00:04:58,060 --> 00:04:59,780
Now that it's come to this,

82
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:01,180
three daifuku won't be enough

83
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:03,580
to heal the wounds in my heart.

84
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:05,200
Honestly, Chief, you always...

85
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,660
Saying you think of your
subordinates above all else...

86
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:08,360
and yet, after saying that,

87
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:11,140
your actions are completely different!

88
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:13,860
Someone who actually cares
about their subordinates

89
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:16,040
shouldn't let them go hungry, should they?

90
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,080
Fine.

91
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:20,140
I'll pay you 10,000 yen, food included.

92
00:05:20,740 --> 00:05:21,820
Really, Chief?

93
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:22,400
Yes.

94
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:25,080
But I'm not giving you
any cash right here and now.

95
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:26,060
W-why not?

96
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:27,440
Because it's you.

97
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:31,480
If I hand you cash,
you'll just blow it on fun again right away.

98
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:33,060
He's got a point.

99
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:35,900
That's always your pattern, senior.

100
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:40,020
Then how are you going
to pay the 10,000 yen?

101
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:42,180
It's this.

102
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,980
All-you-can-eat world cuisine!

103
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:50,580
I'll cover 10,000 yen
worth of admission here.

104
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:52,460
Yay, you're so reasonable!

105
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:54,680
Chief, let's go right now!

106
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,740
Wait, look here.

107
00:05:57,460 --> 00:06:00,460
There are still five days until it opens!

108
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:22,120
So this is the famous Sky Building 50

109
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:25,720
It's packed today, as expected.

110
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:32,960
So these are the people here for it. Speaking of which,
Ryotsu's so hungry he can't walk.

111
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:36,460
You said you'd come from the dorm
on Honda-san's motorbike, though.

112
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:50,180
We've arrived, boss Ryotsu.
I'm so hungry it hurts.

113
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:55,400
What a sorry state.
Pull yourself together and let's go.

114
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:02,920
Honestly, I can't believe your body
held up on water alone for five days.

115
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,980
It was all for this day.

116
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:08,980
For 10,000 yen,
I'll eat 100,000 yen's worth, you'll see.

117
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:14,220
Make sure you actually pay the 10,000 yen.

118
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:15,960
Got it, got it.

119
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:17,300
Here's 10,000 yen.

120
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:24,420
I'm sorry, but with consumption tax,
it comes to 10,000 yen and 635 yen.

121
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,380
So you're saying that's not enough?

122
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,040
Too bad, Ryotsu.

123
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:31,600
I said I'd pay exactly 10,000 yen.

124
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,980
How cheap can you get? Where does it
say all-you-can-eat for 10,000 yen?

125
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:36,940
Well...

126
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,180
Here you go.

127
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,040
If it's come to this, I'll eat the
consumption tax's worth too, just you watch.

128
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:56,920
This one's the best.

129
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,140
You're tough

130
00:07:58,140 --> 00:08:00,460
Shut up!

131
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:07,780
You've gotta take the money, you know.

132
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:10,040
This one's the best.

133
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:12,900
Shut up!

134
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:13,960
Shut up!

135
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:14,640
Shut up!

136
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:16,540
Shut up!

137
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:16,840
Shut up!

138
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:17,440
Shut up!

139
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,600
Shut up!

140
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:20,800
Shut up!

141
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:21,280
Shut up!

142
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:21,940
Shut up!

143
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:22,380
Shut up!

144
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:23,640
Shut up!

145
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:24,680
Stop it, you idiot!

146
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:28,060
But you've gathered quite a lot here,
haven't you?

147
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:29,600
It's perfect.

148
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:31,980
I've never eaten any of these.

149
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:35,520
Come on,
the specialty dishes from around the world

150
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:37,880
are all here on this floor.

151
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:40,620
There is no time limit.

152
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:43,140
Please take your time and enjoy your meal.

153
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:05,800
This looks delicious!

154
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,120
Nice!

155
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:14,200
Eat the good-looking food, even if
you have to push people out of the way.

156
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:16,040
This is my way of doing things.

157
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:21,780
This is a big deal!

158
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,500
That's a huge portion, isn't it?

159
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:30,880
Naturally, it's a waste of time
to keep going back for more.

160
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:33,160
There's no time limit, you know.

161
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:38,700
Aaaaaaah!

162
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:40,340
Aaaaaaah!

163
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,620
This isn't a game!

164
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:52,360
Come on, gourmet senpai,
please come with me to the buffet for real.

165
00:09:52,900 --> 00:10:00,720
What, you can't go alone? You're acting like a girl!
Please, it's so big in there, I'm going to get lost!

166
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:05,840
Senpai, how would I know?
Isn't that just how it goes?

167
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:10,160
Ugh, ugh, ugh, ugh... Fine, what can you do!

168
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,060
Listen, at a buffet,
the good stuff disappears fast!

169
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:16,280
This is the first move! Hurry up!

170
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:17,560
One more plate!

171
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:20,700
What did you say?

172
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:25,960
No way! That's impossible!

173
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:37,580
Hurry! Hurry!

174
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:41,900
An emergency has just
occurred inside this building.

175
00:10:43,460 --> 00:10:44,400
Emergency.

176
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:50,720
We've received word that a fire broke out
at the thermal power plant on the 35th floor.

177
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:53,280
A thermal power plant?

178
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:55,160
Why would there be something like that here?

179
00:10:55,740 --> 00:10:57,960
For now there's no cause for concern,

180
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,940
but we must consider
the worst-case scenario.

181
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:03,360
Please leave your food as
it is and calmly evacuate.

182
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:06,280
This has turned into quite a serious situation,
hasn't it.

183
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:10,020
Let's help guide everyone to evacuate.

184
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:13,500
Everyone,
please stay calm and act carefully.

185
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,140
Calmly, in order, to the elevator.

186
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:21,060
There's no need to panic, it's all right.

187
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,260
There's plenty of time, so stay calm.

188
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:29,820
Sorry, senpai.

189
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:32,100
I went and ate two more plates, you know.

190
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,120
We're heading back, hurry up!

191
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:34,460
Yes.

192
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,740
We're the last ones, then.

193
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:42,400
Thank you all very much
for your cooperation.

194
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:50,400
Now, this elevator is
going to be closed off.

195
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:15,120
Speaking of which,
I didn't see Senpai or Honda-san anywhere.

196
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:18,580
Knowing those guys,
they probably bolted first.

197
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:22,900
Honestly,
those two aren't fit to be police officers.

198
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:25,020
You'd leave all this food
right in front of you?

199
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,340
It's hopeless, run!

200
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,420
Evacuate! Evacuate now!

201
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:49,840
What is this building? It's like a maze!

202
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,440
Senpai, this way!

203
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,960
Hurry, the food's going to be gone!

204
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:57,420
If it's all gone, it's your fault, you know.

205
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:58,520
Then you'd better be prepared.

206
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:02,420
What? Everyone's gone!

207
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,480
Really.

208
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:10,800
Well, whatever. Now's our chance.
Alright, let's eat!

209
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:13,620
Yes! All you can take!

210
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:05,400
Ending

211
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:06,380
There's still some in there.

212
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:16,920
Eat the expensive stuff first,
like foie gras and caviar.

213
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:17,400
Yes.

214
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:19,940
Isn't it kind of smoky?

215
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:21,320
Now that you mention it.

216
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:23,580
They're probably running
some attraction outside.

217
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:25,260
Maybe so.

218
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:29,220
Geez, so noisy during a nice meal.

219
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:30,720
Hello?

220
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:32,260
It's Ryotsu!

221
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,260
You surprised me, is this the Chief?

222
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:41,420
Listen carefully, there's been a fire
on the 35th floor of that building.

223
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:43,340
That building is on fire.

224
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:48,140
Come on, Chief,
I'm not falling for that lie.

225
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:49,740
It's not a lie.

226
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:53,960
Chief, I paid 635 yen, you know.

227
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:58,860
I'll eat every bit of my 10,000 yen worth before I leave.
You'll be amazed!

228
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:06,720
It really is a fire!

229
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:11,060
You two are the only ones
still in the building.

230
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,260
Everyone else evacuated long ago.

231
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,060
I'm really scared!

232
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,060
We're going to end up as yakitori!

233
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:18,700
Stay calm, you too.

234
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,200
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

235
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,380
The elevators can't be used anymore.

236
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,280
Until we come to rescue you from here.

237
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:25,880
Stay put and wait without panicking.

238
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:27,060
Understood, Ryotsu?

239
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:28,900
Don't you dare act on your own.

240
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:31,180
We're trapped.

241
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,620
Don't panic, Honda!

242
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,040
That's undignified!

243
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:36,660
Just wait a moment.

244
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:38,100
Where do you think you're going?

245
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,780
Senpai, please don't leave us behind!

246
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:42,420
First, let's secure a fire extinguisher.

247
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:50,940
If we close the fire shutter,
the fire can't get in for now.

248
00:15:50,940 --> 00:15:53,200
In the meantime, let's eat.

249
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,940
You're still going to eat in this situation?

250
00:15:56,380 --> 00:15:59,500
I came here planning to
eat 100,000 yen's worth.

251
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:02,180
I paid 635 yen, after all.

252
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,760
No matter what, I'm going to eat.

253
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,700
This is a live report from
the Sky Building fire scene.

254
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:13,600
Two people are still inside.

255
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:16,280
We've just spotted the two of them.

256
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:18,540
They're eating.

257
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:21,080
What an idiot.

258
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:23,340
Ryo-tsume is smiling and eating!

259
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:26,900
Because our senior is the type
who doesn't get rattled by anything.

260
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:44,900
What was that explosion just now?

261
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:47,680
The gas station two floors down exploded.

262
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:50,600
Why is there something
like that in a building?

263
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:58,040
The electrical system's gone haywire,
damn it.

264
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:01,800
Cold, cold!

265
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:04,480
The fire's spreading faster now.

266
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,580
Eat faster.

267
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:07,160
I can't eat like this!

268
00:17:09,298 --> 00:17:12,440
the fire shutter...

269
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:14,100
Stop making such a racket, will you?

270
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:19,360
Well, this'll do for now.

271
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:32,560
Shut up! I can't eat in peace! Honestly!

272
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:52,720
Hurry and come save us!

273
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,960
This meat's almost done, just a little more

274
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:02,220
you know.

275
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:03,400
Aaaaaah!

276
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:07,880
It's hopeless, there's no fire extinguisher!

277
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,520
Let's see if there's
anything in the kitchen.

278
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:13,480
Here's something good!

279
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,960
Come on, bring over the soup, chop chop!

280
00:18:19,460 --> 00:18:21,020
Okay, I don't have a
fire extinguisher either.

281
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:22,580
This'll smother the fire.

282
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:23,220
Here goes!

283
00:18:25,060 --> 00:18:26,900
Idiot, this is oil!

284
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:29,720
I'm done with you.

285
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:31,140
You're still eating?

286
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:33,040
About two minutes. Can you hear me?

287
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,980
A rescue helicopter is
heading for the rooftop.

288
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:39,340
There's an emergency staircase
at the back of the kitchen.

289
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:41,720
You should be able to
reach the rooftop from there.

290
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:42,960
Head there right away.

291
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:45,100
Yay!

292
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:47,660
Yes, I'm still going to eat plenty more!

293
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:50,120
If it comes to that,
I'll take the whole thing with me.

294
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:53,800
Let's leave the food and run!

295
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:54,880
We're done for!

296
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:57,420
Please.

297
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:04,740
Oh no, it's no good, the fire!

298
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,580
Nonsense, we'll break through by force!

299
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:10,460
Let's go!

300
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:19,800
Wait, I need the dessert that
covers the consumption tax.

301
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:20,840
Let's get out of here quickly!

302
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:28,980
I wonder if Yo-chan and
the others are all right.

303
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:52,780
I forgot to mention, there's a world
fireworks expo happening on the rooftop.

304
00:19:52,780 --> 00:19:53,500
Be careful!

305
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:55,320
Why does it have to be now?

306
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:11,460
Ugh!

307
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,340
Ugh!

308
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:13,380
Ugh!

309
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:13,720
Ugh!

310
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,060
Ugh!

311
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:20,260
Don't come any closer than that!

312
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:22,020
Jump across from there!

313
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:22,940
What?

314
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:25,380
We carried it all the way up here!

315
00:20:25,820 --> 00:20:27,000
Are we leaving this behind?

316
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:27,900
Hurry up.

317
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:28,660
Hurry!

318
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:29,500
Ugh!

319
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:31,000
If it comes to this, there's no helping it.

320
00:20:32,460 --> 00:20:33,700
Are you planning to take all that with you?

321
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:34,660
Don't be ridiculous.

322
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:38,560
Caviar in my pockets,

323
00:20:39,220 --> 00:20:40,900
and escargot in my pants.

324
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:48,220
Alright, that's exactly 100,000 yen's worth.

325
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,500
Can you really jump
across dressed like that?

326
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:53,340
Nothing is impossible for me.

327
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:55,260
Alright, Honda, go first.

328
00:20:55,260 --> 00:21:02,720
Hurry up!

329
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:03,180
Yes.

330
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:07,080
You can see it, right?

331
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:19,040
!

332
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,520
Anytime! I'll do it myself!

333
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:23,260
No, I refuse! Forget it!

334
00:21:30,740 --> 00:21:31,920
Alright, you're next!

335
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:34,100
Leave that food behind!

336
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:35,280
No way!

337
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:37,060
I'll eat this much!

338
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:46,140
Gramps!

339
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:46,980
Ryo-chan!

340
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:53,960
I managed to catch hold!

341
00:21:55,260 --> 00:21:56,580
But it's heavy!

342
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:00,260
It's going to snap!
Quick, throw away that food!

343
00:22:00,260 --> 00:22:02,760
No way, I can't do that!

344
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:05,880
Hauling out that much food is impossible!

345
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:08,820
This is where true character shows.

346
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:12,600
Are you really going to throw
your life away for food, Ryotsu?

347
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:27,340
Aaaaaah!

348
00:22:27,340 --> 00:22:35,440
Aaaaaah! They fell into the water!

349
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:36,200
Aaaaaah!

350
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:40,180
Can't be helped.

351
00:22:40,180 --> 00:22:40,960
Eeeeeeh!

352
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,900
I used a tablecloth as a parachute!

353
00:22:51,900 --> 00:22:53,980
Impressive, senpai. That's not
something a normal person could do.

354
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:19,840
So frustrating!

355
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:23,760
Escargot and lobster too,

356
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:28,320
I went to all that trouble bringing them,
and now they're all scattered!

357
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:32,580
And I haven't even eaten
10,000 yen's worth yet!

358
00:23:33,160 --> 00:23:36,780
This guy apparently values
food more than his own life.

359
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:40,940
Chief, pay for me one more
time and take me to the buffet!

360
00:23:40,940 --> 00:23:42,560
How would I know, you idiot!

361
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:45,600
Guun-dei! Guun-dei!

362
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,380
Guun-dei! Guun-dei!

363
00:23:48,580 --> 00:23:50,820
Guun-dei! Guun-dei!

364
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:05,840
Whoa! Shiratori Reiji!

365
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:07,707
Your father was moved by you,

366
00:24:07,757 --> 00:24:10,820
weren't you supposed to become
a super-duper poor person?

367
00:24:11,820 --> 00:24:13,680
Did you come to invite
me on another frozen date?

368
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:15,280
French food, you say?

369
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:17,060
I'm coming along too!

370
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:20,100
Next time, his return! Shiratori Reiji!

371
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:21,220
Nice to meet you!

372
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
through a harsh desert,

373
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,160
I want to be freer than a bird.

374
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,100
A lady's dreams changing at
the speed of a kaleidoscope.

375
00:25:07,100 --> 00:25:07,600
me

376
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:09,900
me

377
00:25:11,100 --> 00:25:12,600
me

378
00:25:12,600 --> 00:25:13,300
me

379
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:23,200
me

380
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:25,780
me

381
00:25:25,780 --> 00:25:27,900
me

382
00:25:27,900 --> 00:25:29,440
me

383
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:29,860
me

384
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:36,560
me

385
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:36,580
me

386
00:25:36,580 --> 00:25:36,600
me

387
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:41,020
Thank you for watching.

